# The changelog is append-only: every branch adds its own bullet to the same
# section, so a plain merge reports a conflict on essentially every pull
# request even though the correct resolution is always "keep both bullets".
# The union driver does exactly that and is built into git, needing no
# configuration on anyone's machine.
#
# Resolving these by hand is not merely tedious, it has been wrong: diff3-style
# conflicts add a `||||||| <sha>` base marker on top of the usual three, and two
# of those reached main inside this file before anyone noticed.
docs/CHANGELOG.md merge=union
